      "worked_solution": "The length of the semi-minor axis is half the length of the minor axis.\n\n- The minor axis is the shortest diameter of the ellipse, which is the line segment bounded by the points $(-3,1)$ and $(1,1).$ So, the length of the minor axis is $1-(-3)=4.$\n\n- The length of the semi-minor axis, then, is $\\frac{4}{2}=2.$",
